  "limitations": [
    "This is a dated physical-channel mapping snapshot. USB COM numbers can change again after reconnection; it does not assert the present port names after subsequent user moves.",
    "PPK serials and calibration modifiers come from the accepted first-batch endpoint metadata and the supplied premise that COM10/COM11 remain those same PPKs; this offline audit does not enumerate live USB devices.",
    "No new IEEE/silicon identity was read. Mapping COM16 to the historical TX supply channel and COM14 to the historical RX supply channel does not independently read or authenticate the MCU identity.",
    "Counter anomalies occur in RX-off windows and are reported. They are not repaired, and no loss percentage or waveform-wide integrity claim is inferred. Robust medians establish a supply-current step, not precision energy or time alignment.",
    "Direct ADC medians can differ slightly from the original ppk2-api filtered medians near range changes. Both methods lead to the same channel mapping.",
    "The script requests RX state changes only; this audit does not independently monitor radiated RF."
  ]
